ription":"Dutch colony in Southeast Asia and Oceania (1800–1949)","inception":1800,"dissolved":1949.986301369863,"enwiki":"Dutch East Indies","summary":"The Dutch East Indies was a colony of the Dutch Empire, established in 1800 when the Batavian Republic took control of the Dutch East India Company. In 1824, Dutch Malacca was ceded to Britain, and is now part of modern Malaysia, with most of the rest becoming Indonesia in August 1945. During the 19th century, Dutch forces fought a series of wars against indigenous states which greatly expanded the Dutch East Indies. Dutch rule reached its greatest territorial extent in the early 20th century with the occupation of Western New Guinea."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q5317276","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q188161","value_label":"Dutch East Indies","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P156","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dutch East Indies"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q768372","value_label":"Dirk Fock","from_t":1921.2246575342465,"to_t":1926.6794520547944,"title":"head of state","property":"P35","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dirk Fock"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q1199713","value_label":"Batavia","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Batavia"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q7411","value_label":"Dutch","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dutch"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q7411","value_label":"Dutch","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Dutch"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q3233989","value_label":"Lanfang Republic","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P155","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Lanfang Republic"},{"qid":"Q188161","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q20427320","value_label":"Soppeng Sultanate","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"prope